The Niimura main house's cherry, the one tree left in this land.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This little settlement had gone on for 800 years without ever being ruled by anyone.<PG>
Wasn't that, maybe, a miracle?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Or had there been some wisdom that worked that miracle?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Wasn't there something, even now, that kept handing that wisdom down?<PG>
Might there be something in the storehouse's books?
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Something that could become the wisdom to help <STYLE ID="2">Sakura</STYLE>...<PG>
In the Arata settlement, customs from overseas survive, deeply rooted.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
And not just customs. The color of <STYLE ID="2">Sakura's</STYLE> eyes and hair tells the same story.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Even now, as a throwback, a child with a foreigner's looks is born from time to time.<PG>
I've heard that the existence of gods, devils, witches, and shinigami was passed on at that time too, by the Westerners.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
But there was something else that had been passed on.<PG>
